---
title: "You're Registered - The Zero Fog"
permalink: /confirmation/
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head_extras %}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<meta name="description" content="You're registered for the free Zero Fog workshop. Here's what happens next.">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_css %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/pages/confirmation-3.css' | v }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<a href="/" class="brand">The Zero Fog</a>
<button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" onclick="toggleTheme()">Light</button>

<main class="content">

  <p class="reg-greeting hidden" id="regGreeting">Hey, <span id="regName"></span></p>

  <h1 class="ty-headline">You're registered. Check your email for the details.</h1>

  <p class="ty-sub">Your workshop access link is on its way - usually lands in your inbox within 2 minutes.</p>

  <p class="reg-details hidden" id="regDetails">We sent it to <strong id="regEmail"></strong>.</p>

  {# The time they picked, echoed back. Revealed by JS from the `when` parameter our schedule
     step passes - the exact label they saw when choosing, in their own timezone. #}
  <p class="reg-details hidden" id="regSlot"></p>

  {# The personal join link. Revealed only when a token is present, and built by JS from our own
     origin rather than from a parameter, so a crafted URL cannot repoint it.
     Inline styles on purpose: keeps confirmation-3.css untouched, which the cache-rename rule
     in this project makes expensive to change. #}
  <div style="text-align:center;margin:28px 0 8px;">
    <a href="#" id="regJoin" class="hidden" style="display:inline-block;background:var(--accent);color:#0d0d0d;font-weight:800;font-size:1rem;padding:16px 32px;border-radius:10px;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Open my session</a>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text2);margin-top:10px;">This is your personal link - keep it. It also arrives by email.</p>
  </div>



  <div class="device-msg hidden" id="deviceDesktop">
    <p class="device-title">You're on a desktop - perfect.</p>
    <p class="device-text">Add the workshop to your calendar now. The join link is in the email we just sent - open it on your computer when it's time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="device-msg hidden" id="deviceMobile">
    <p class="device-title">You're on mobile - the workshop link is in your email.</p>
    <p class="device-text">For the best experience, join from a desktop or laptop when it starts. You'll see the slides, demos, and Q&amp;A in full.</p>
  </div>

  {# Calendar buttons: revealed by JS only when the `slot` parameter carries a usable start time.
     Hidden on direct visits, which is every visit that did not come through the schedule step. #}
  <div class="cal-btns hidden" id="calBtns">
    <a class="cal-btn" id="calGoogle" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Add to Google Calendar</a>
    <a class="cal-btn" id="calIcs" href="#" download="the-zero-fog-workshop.ics">Apple / Outlook (.ics)</a>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="steps-section">

    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <p class="step-title">Check your inbox right now.</p>
        <p class="step-text">Look for "Zero Fog" in your sender list. If it's not there within 2 minutes, check your Promotions or Spam folder and move it to your main inbox.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <p class="step-title">Mark it "not spam" and move to inbox.</p>
        <p class="step-text">This is critical. If you don't, the next email - the one with your workshop link - won't reach you. Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo - they all filter aggressively.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <p class="step-title">Show up to the workshop.</p>
        <p class="step-text">Attendees who stay to the end get 3 free bonuses delivered right after. Skip the workshop and you skip those too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="bullets-section">
    <p class="bullets-heading">Attend, and you'll also get:</p>

    <div class="bonus-grid">
      <div class="bonus-card">
        <img class="bonus-cover" src="/assets/img/bonus-cover-01-caffeine.webp" alt="Your Caffeine Blueprint - cutoff window calculator" width="480" height="640" loading="lazy">
        <span class="bonus-name">Your Caffeine Blueprint</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bonus-card">
        <img class="bonus-cover" src="/assets/img/bonus-cover-03-mistakes.webp" alt="10 Recovery Mistakes - myths debunked" width="480" height="640" loading="lazy">
        <span class="bonus-name">10 Recovery Mistakes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bonus-card">
        <img class="bonus-cover" src="/assets/img/bonus-cover-02-recovery.webp" alt="The Recovery Protocol - five changes" width="480" height="640" loading="lazy">
        <span class="bonus-name">The Recovery Protocol</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="bonus-note">Delivered to your inbox right after you watch.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="credibility">
    <p class="credibility-text">I work from home. For 3 years I ran on coffee and willpower. Brain fog, bad decisions, crashed by 2 PM every day. I tried everything - morning routines, productivity systems, supplements. None of it lasted. Then I found what was actually broken - and fixed it in weeks. This workshop is the thing I wish someone had showed me 3 years ago.</p>
    <p class="credibility-author">- Kirill, The Zero Fog</p>
  </div>

  <div class="final-cta">
    <p>Check your email - we'll see you inside.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="disclaimer">This is an educational program, not medical treatment. Results vary.</p>

</main>

{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/pages/confirmation-2.js' | v }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
